// Apio boards definitions.
// These FPGAs are referred to from boards.jsonc and their values are structured
// to match the FpgaDefinition protocol buffer in apio-definitions.proto.
//
// COMMON-FIELDS:
//    'fpga_id': These are the entries keys. They equal to the vendor part
//        converted to lower-case-0-9 with an optional suffix denoting a
//        variant, e.g. '-8k' when oversizing a 4k device to act as a 8k
//        device.
//
//    'arch': The architecture group of the FPGA, This determines the semantic
//        of its fields and the toolchain commands that are used to process it.
// 
//    'vendor-part': The exact and complete part number, without the delivery
//        information such as tape vs tray. This field is used for information 
//        only.
//
//    'size': The device size. This field is used for information only
//
// The reset of the fields are architecture specific and are described in each
// architecture section below.
//
//
// ============= ICE40 ARCHITECTURE
//
// Architecture specific params:
//    'nextpnr-type': The type parameter that is passed to nextpnr.
//    'nextpnr-package': The package parameter that is passed to nextpnr.
//
